 "anatomy-steps": {
  "item/card-1": {
   "steps": [
    {
     "kind": "answer",
     "scope": "Spacing",
     "question": "How dense is the layout?",
     "answer": "Spacious",
     "why": "Big space makes big moments."
    },
    {
     "kind": "answer",
     "scope": "Shape",
     "question": "What should control corners say?",
     "answer": "Pill",
     "why": "Pill controls feel playful."
    },
    {
     "kind": "rule",
     "situation": "items that belong together",
     "use": "space.gap.default",
     "not": "space.gap.tight",
     "why": "Air keeps big type readable."
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "space.inset.container",
     "key": "default.padding",
     "value": "2rem",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "space.32",
     "shares": []
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "space.gap.group",
     "key": "default.gap",
     "value": "2.5rem",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "space.40",
     "shares": []
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "radius.element",
     "key": "radius",
     "value": "0.75rem",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "radius.12: We use the 12px box corner for boxes that grow in order to keep them box-shaped objects by the relation: a pill control gives way to the box corner. A moderate radius does this by curving the corners while the sides stay straight as the box grows. So a text area or a list item stays a box, not an oval, because controls are pills (shape.values) and the brand is bold (brand.q1).",
     "shares": []
    }
   ]
  },
  "item/card-2": {
   "steps": [
    {
     "kind": "answer",
     "scope": "Shape",
     "question": "What should control corners say?",
     "answer": "Pill",
     "why": "Pill controls feel playful."
    },
    {
     "kind": "answer",
     "scope": "Iconography",
     "question": "How big are icons next to text?",
     "answer": "Larger than the text",
     "why": "Larger icons hold their own next to big type."
    },
    {
     "kind": "rule",
     "situation": "corners of buttons and inputs",
     "use": "radius.control (pill)",
     "not": "sharp corners",
     "why": "Pills match the brand's round, playful shapes. Sharp corners would feel corporate."
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "size.control.default",
     "key": "media.icon.size",
     "value": "3.25rem",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "size.52",
     "shares": []
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "radius.control",
     "key": "media.icon.radius",
     "value": "calc(infinity * 1px)",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "radius.pill: We use a pill corner for buttons and inputs in order to mark their role as controls in a playful tone, by brand convention. A full radius does this by rounding both ends into a capsule, the brand's signature shape. So every action feels bold and friendly, because the brand is bold (brand.q1), controls are pills (shape.values) and each section holds one big idea (content.q2).",
     "shares": []
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "color.surface.sunken",
     "key": "media.icon.background",
     "value": "#FCEFE6",
     "darkValue": "#090403",
     "byScheme": true,
     "rule": "A recessed fill, a step below content.",
     "pick": "neutral.100, a step below content (1.13:1 on surface.default), so table headers and wells read as recessed.",
     "darkPick": "neutral.floor: We use the floor step, below the page's canvas, for table headers and wells in dark, in order to show depth by tone, 1.13:1 under content and 1.05:1 under the canvas. The darker fill does this by the depth rule turned downward: what sits lower is darker. So a well reads as recessed and never as a raised card, because dark ships as standard (theming.values) and depth reads from tone and lines (elevation.definition).",
     "shares": [
      "surface.highlight",
      "action.secondary.hover",
      "category.5.subtle",
      "disabled.surface"
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "token",
     "semantic": "size.icon",
     "key": "media.icon.icon-size",
     "value": "1.25rem",
     "byScheme": true,
     "pick": "size.20",
     "shares": []
    }
   ]
